hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"108","\I made my sword in the shape of the sword of Samura ibn Jundub.\"" Samura also claimed that he made his sword in the shape of the sword of Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace)"," for he was a Hanafi."""
"109","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) wore two coats of mail on the Day of \nUhud"," so he tried to climb the boulder but was not able. He therefore made Talha sit\nbeneath him"," and the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace)"," climbed up until he stood upright on the rock.\"" He said: \""I heard the Prophet say (Allah bless him and give\nhim peace): 'Talha performed a deed worthy of reward'!”"""
